abstract: >
  Wavewell is a browser-based, install-free simulator of electron bound states
  in a GaAs/AlGaAs quantum well. It solves the time-independent Schrödinger
  equation live via Numerov integration with node-counting and bisection
  eigenvalue search. The numerical method is exposed in open, commented source
  so learners can progress from observing energy quantization to modifying the
  algorithm themselves. Wavewell is the pilot module of a three-tier open
  computational-science education pipeline spanning foundational data literacy
  to advanced computational physics, designed for zero-cost adoption by
  under-resourced institutions.
